        "answer": "The most common error is making assumptions without explicit, open communication. When students avoid honest conversations due to fear of awkwardness or conflict, minor friction compounds into major resentment. Establishing mutual expectations early prevents unnecessary misunderstandings. Respecting smartphone privacy, refraining from digital surveillance, and addressing insecurities directly in person fosters authentic, mature campus intimacy."
